    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** headlining the roster, sporting our highest efficiency score of 84.24. The combination of a favorable matchup against Baz and a significant +16% park adjustment makes **Junior Caminero** an automatic start in the 3-hole. We are also leaning heavily into stolen base upside today; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.45) is a priority play because he faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, and his lead-off spot against Miller, B allows him to maximize his elite speed profile. Furthermore, **Caleb Durbin** (70.40) benefits from the day's softest opposing arm, Wilkinson (xERA 8.21), providing a significant 19% boost to his efficiency that makes him a core component of today's lineup.\n\nWe remain cautious with **Yordan Alvarez** (56.07), who faces a suboptimal L/L platoon matchup against Basso; while his elite xwOBA keeps him viable, he is effectively skating on thin ice compared to **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.05), who is thriving with excellent park and skill adjustments despite a lower batting order slot. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (44.02), who missed the cut strictly due to limited availability in the lineup and a harsh L/L platoon penalty against Newcomb, S. While **Carson Benge** hovered near the marginal threshold, he could not displace **Chase Meidroth** (42.69) or the other higher-upside bats, as our roster depth dictates prioritizing efficiency over raw talent. Monitor the late-inning weather, but the core objective remains the same: leverage the speed of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to secure the SB category while **Kyle Schwarber** anchors the power output from the top of the order.",
